From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:03:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(delegation): delegate_task action=transcript reads a
 child's steps

A parent could see a subagent's progress only through the live .log paths in the spawn result, which sit in the gateway's cache and are out of reach when the parent's terminal runs on another machine, and are gone after 7 days. delegate_task(action='transcript', subagent_id=... | delegation_id=..., task_index=...) now returns the child's stored session as entries (assistant text, thinking, tool calls with arguments, tool results cut with their full size, times) with status and running, newest limit entries by default, after= to read on, max_chars to bound a page. It works for running and finished children of the caller's own spawn tree only (live registry ownership, or the stored row's ancestry), masks credentials like the live log, and falls back to the task's log only for a delegation whose manifest names the caller as owner. The manifest now records the owner session and each task's subagent_id. The spawn result's live_transcripts_hint points to the action.
